WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Hi there, Shankar here. We're about to celebrate Thanksgiving in the US and we thought we'd mark the moment with a question. Who are you most grateful for? Maybe it's a family member or a dear friend or maybe it's a stranger who helped you in a moment of crisis. Our sister podcast, My Unsung Hero, is all about stories of people like this. Thanksgiving happens once a year. Please subscribe to My Unsung Hero so you can feel the warm glow of Thanksgiving every week of the year. Today's story comes from Tony Ludlow.
大家好，我是尚卡尔。我们即将在美国庆祝感恩节，我们想用一个问题来纪念这个时刻。你最感激谁？也许是一位家庭成员、一位亲密的朋友，或者是在你陷入危机时伸出援手的陌生人。我们的姊妹播客《我的幕后英雄》讲述的全都是这样的人的故事。感恩节一年只有一次。请订阅《我的幕后英雄》，这样你一年中的每周都能感受到感恩节的温暖。今天的故事来自托尼·勒德洛。

2
00:00:42.000 --> 00:01:35.000
When Tony was in eighth grade at a school in Fortsmouth, Arkansas, he had an English teacher named Cecil Holman. She was the first black woman he had ever had as a teacher. In fact, she was the first black woman with whom he had ever had a conversation. She left such an impression on him that he still vividly remembers what she looked like. She was immaculately dressed and she wore kind of large floral print dresses, everything about her said class and dignity and she had a particular perfume that she wore that just seemed to fit. That spring she began to teach the class about poetry. And I started to tank. I hated it. That spring should begin to teach the class about poetry. And I started to tank. I hated it. His grades were falling. So Mrs. Holman told him he had to stay after school to get extra
当托尼在阿肯色州普茨茅斯的一所学校上八年级时，他有一位名叫塞西尔·霍尔曼的英语老师。她是托尼遇到的第一位黑人女老师。事实上，她是托尼与之交谈过的第一位黑人女老师。她给托尼留下了如此深刻的印象，以至于他至今仍清晰地记得她的长相。她衣着无可挑剔，总是穿着那种大印花连衣裙，她的一切都散发着优雅和尊严，她身上有一种独特的香水味，恰到好处。那年春天，她开始给全班讲授诗歌。而我的成绩开始一落千丈。我讨厌诗歌。那年春天她开始给全班讲授诗歌。而我的成绩开始一落千丈。我讨厌诗歌。他的成绩在下降。于是霍尔曼太太告诉他，他必须放学后留下来接受额外的

3
00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:08.000
help. And I didn't like Mrs. Holman. I hated her for keeping me from being able to play sports. And so I was angry at her. Well, one day I said, I was just, I was just fed up and I said, Mrs. Holman, I don't relate to any of this stuff. Poetry stuff like girls would write it's about daffodils and butterflies and stuff like that, unicorns. I don't relate to any of this stuff and I'm sure that none of the male members of my family
辅导。而我当时并不喜欢霍尔曼太太。我恨她剥夺了我参加体育运动的时间。所以我对她满腔怒火。有一天，我说，我实在是受够了，我说，霍尔曼太太，我对这些东西一点也产生不了共鸣。诗歌这东西就像女孩子写的，讲的全是水仙花、蝴蝶之类的东西，还有独角兽。我对这些东西完全没有共鸣，而且我确信我家里所有的男性

4
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:42.000
have any use for poetry. So the next day I had to go back to her class again, and she handed me a book. And she said, I want you to take this book and I'll put a bookmark in there. And I want you to go home. I want you to take this book and I put a bookmark in there and I want you to go home. I want you to read this poem and then and this was on a Monday then on Friday I want you to tell me what the poem was about. Well, I hated the whole idea and so I reluctantly went home and opened the book to read Eulisys
都对诗歌毫无兴趣。所以第二天我不得不再次去她的课堂，她递给我一本书。她说，我要你拿走这本书，我在里面放了一个书签。我要你回家去。我要你拿走这本书，我在里面放了一个书签，我要你回家去。我要你读这首诗，然后——这是在星期一——到了星期五，我要你告诉我这首诗讲的是什么。嗯，我讨厌这个主意，所以我勉强回到家，翻开书阅读阿尔弗雷德·丁尼生勋爵的

5
00:02:42.000 --> 00:03:42.000
by Alfred Lord Tennyson, and it changed my life. And she started to give me more poems like that. I read Invictus, and if, and Dolcea deumest and poems written by men about the lives that they were living, and it just absolutely changed my life. At the end of the school year, she went around the classroom and shook everyone's hand and said, good luck next year and all of those things. And then when she came to me, she took my hand and she leaned in forward real close to me. And she said, Tony Ludlow, I expect greatness from you. And I'd never heard anybody challenge me
《尤利西斯》，它改变了我的人生。接着她开始给我更多这样的诗。我读了《不可战胜》、《如果》以及《死得其所》，还有男人们为自己所经历的生活而写的诗，这绝对彻底改变了我的人生。学年结束时，她走过教室，和每个人握手，说着“祝你明年好运”之类的话。然后当她走到我面前时，她握住我的手，身体向前倾，离我非常近。她说，托尼·勒德洛，我对你寄予厚望。我这辈子从来没有听过任何人向我发起过

6
00:03:42.000 --> 00:04:14.000
with that kind of thing in my whole life. that he challenged me with that kind of thing in my whole life. Fast forward, after 10 years in the Marine Corps, I went to college, and I was a double major in English and history. I was a major in English because of Mrs. Holman. I never got a chance to tell her any of these things. She passed away the year I graduated from high school. I never knew it. I didn't know about her passing.
这种挑战。快进到在海军陆战队服役10年之后，我上了大学，并且主修英语和历史双学位。我主修英语全是因为霍尔曼太太。我从来没有机会把这些事告诉她。就在我高中毕业的那一年，她去世了。我当时并不知道。我不知道她已经离世了。

7
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.000
But years later, many years later, in fact, just a few years ago, I connected with her niece and we have become family. Sherry Tollver is her name. And Sherry and I have become family because we both love Mrs. Cecil Holman, my eighth grade English teacher, my unsung hero. Tony Ladlow of Memphis, Tennessee. He went on to become a teacher of American history in English, and he taught for almost 20 years. For many more stories like this, be sure to follow our sister podcast, My Unsung Hero. I'm Shankar Vedantam. See you soon. Afiyet olsun. There aren't comments yet for this episode. Click on any sentence in the transcript to leave a comment.
但多年以后，很多年以后，其实就在几年前，我和她的侄女取得了联系，我们成了家人。她叫雪莉·托尔弗。雪莉和我之所以成为了家人，是因为我们都深爱着塞西尔·霍尔曼太太——我的八年级英语老师，我的幕后英雄。我是来自田纳西州孟菲斯的托尼·拉德洛。他后来成为了一名美国历史和英语老师，教书近二十年。想听更多类似的故事，请务必关注我们的姊妹播客《我的幕后英雄》。我是尚卡尔·韦丹塔姆。再见。祝您胃口好。这一集目前还没有评论。点击文稿中的任何句子即可发表评论。
